  "name": "Cook Finance IssuanceModuleV2 caller-chosen weightings",
  "summary": "IssuanceModuleV2.issueWithSingleToken2() takes caller-supplied component weightings without checking them, multiplies the issue quantity by each weighting and trades that much of the CKToken's own holdings through a Pancake adapter with no minimum output. Attackers seeded thin Pancake pools between components, issued one wei with a weighting equal to almost all of the CKToken's balance of a component, so the module swapped those holdings into their pools, then removed the liquidity and sold the components; four CKTokens were drained.",
